      <li class="buds-faq__item" role="listitem" data-category="category3"> <h3 class="buds-faq__question"> <button type="button" class="buds-faq__button" data-omni-type="microsite_contentinter" data-omni="gbuds4pro:features:faq:acdn-open:galaxy-experience^auto-switch" ga-ca="content click" ga-ac="accordion" ga-la="gbuds4pro:features:faq:acdn-open:galaxy-experience^auto-switch" data-keyword="auto-switch" aria-expanded="false" data-di-id="di-id-55f4e66-9bafb913" data-media-group="interest" data-media-details="gbuds4pro:features:faq:acdn-open:galaxy-experience^auto-switch" data-media-action="click"> <span class="buds-faq__text">What are the benefits of using Auto Switch on Galaxy Buds4 Pro?</span> 
         <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-di-res-id="fb6cedd5-73ed07da" data-di-rand="1778922042993"> 
          <use xlink:href="#icon-arrow-down" href="#icon-arrow-down"></use> 
         </svg> </button> </h3> 
       <div class="buds-faq__answer js-faq-answer" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"> 
        <div class="buds-faq__answer-inner"> 
         <p class="buds-faq__description"> Auto Switch uses Bluetooth to automatically deliver the audio source between the devices. The feature allows you to take incoming calls while you're working on a creative project on your Galaxy Tab or Galaxy Book. Once the call is over, you can go right back to your project effortlessly.<sup><a href="#desc-section" class="click_sup" title="See Disclaimer" data-sup-tag="sup-25" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-di-id="di-id-7f2e7279-2b016c50">27</a></sup> </p> 
        </div> 
       </div> </li> 
